  "_style": "Address the user with informal “sən” everywhere (Yadda saxla, Göndər, sənin, səni); never “siz”. Speak to the couple as “ikiniz / ikinizin / birlikdə” and use 2nd-person plural verbs only when a line clearly addresses both of you (“İkiniz də cavab verdiniz”). The other person is always “partnyorun / partnyoruna / partnyorunla”; Azerbaijani has no grammatical gender, so use “o” or impersonal phrasing and never words that assume gender or relationship type (sevgilin, ərin, arvadın, oğlan/qız yoldaşın, həyat yoldaşın). Never attach a case or possessive suffix to a name placeholder (%@) because vowel harmony cannot be predicted: rephrase instead (“Göndərən: %@”, “%@ səni düşünür”, “%@ ilə bağlandın” → “Partnyorun: %@”). The same goes for Coupley: prefer “Coupley tətbiqində” over adding a suffix. Quotes are curly “ ” (inner ‘ ’); ellipsis is the single character “…”; no space before . , : ; ! ?; keep “ · ”, \\n and every placeholder exactly. Numbers: decimal comma, thin/regular space for thousands (1 250), ordinals with a hyphen (5-ci ildönümü, 2026-cı il); dates as “14 noyabr 2026” with lowercase month and weekday names. Nouns stay singular after numbers (%lld gün, %lld xatirə, %lld ağac), so plural categories are [\"one\",\"other\"] and both usually carry the same text. Buttons and short actions are short imperatives in sən-form (Yadda saxla, Ləğv et, Yenidən cəhd et, Əlaqəni kəs); never infinitive -maq/-mək on buttons. Titles, tabs, buttons and chips use sentence case (only the first word capitalized: Günün sualı, Reklamları sil, Xatirə kapsulu) except proper names like Coupley, Premium, CoupleSync. Latin script only: use ə (U+0259, never ä), ğ, ı, İ, ö, ü, ç, ş and respect dotted/dotless i in capitals (i → İ, ı → I). AI is “Sİ” (süni intellekt). Tone is warm, light and natural, like a good Azerbaijani app; avoid literal calques and cheesy phrasing.",
